@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@adminEmail = suadmintaxi@gmail.com
@adminPassword = Admin@123

### Set from list responses or MongoDB
@driverId = 69cf96bf2fdb2596603b3f15
@documentId = REPLACE_WITH_DOCUMENT_OBJECT_ID

# --- How to avoid "Invalid or expired token" ---
# 1) Send "Admin login" below FIRST (same file). Token is copied into @adminAccessToken on the next line.
# 2) Then send any GET/PATCH — they use Bearer {{adminAccessToken}} (reliable in REST Client).
# 3) Token expires per JWT_ACCESS_EXPIRES_IN (often 15m) — log in again if needed.
# 4) Postman: ignore @ lines; copy data.accessToken from login JSON into Bearer manually.
# 5) Unique @name avoids clashing with other .http files that also define admin login.

###############################################################################
### Admin login — SEND THIS FIRST
###############################################################################
# @name adminLoginDriverVerification
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

###
# Pull token from login JSON — REST Client needs # @name above (not ###) and .$ in the JSON path
@adminAccessToken = {{adminLoginDriverVerification.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}

###############################################################################
### Driver verification & documents (uses @adminAccessToken from login above)
###############################################################################

### 1) List drivers pending verification
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/drivers/verification
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccessToken}}

### 1b) Same without v1 prefix
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/drivers/verification
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccessToken}}

### 2) List all documents for a driver
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/drivers/69cf96bf2fdb2596603b3f15/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccessToken}}

### 3) Download a document file (redirects to S3 URL)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/documents/69cf9b9af9e52e25555c0f1b/download
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccessToken}}

### 4) Approve document
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/documents/69d349fcc974d09e20111a73/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccessToken}}

{
  "status": "APPROVED"
}

### 5) Reject document (reason required)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/documents/69cf9b9af9e52e25555c0f1b/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccessToken}}

{
  "status": "REJECTED",
  "reason": "Document is blurry; please upload a clearer scan."
}

### 6) Final driver approval — documents OPTIONAL; one click approves account + minimal profile
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/drivers/69cf96bf2fdb2596603b3f15/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccessToken}}

### 6b) Approve driver by email (no document upload needed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/drivers/approve-by-email
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "kiruba.driver@yopmail.com"
}

### 6c) Approve customer by email (Sruthi / any customer)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/customers/approve-by-email
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sruthi.customer@yopmail.com"
}

